\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.2.1}{\ignorespaces The running tree mid-Morris-walk, at the moment \texttt  {cur}~$=4$: two live threads (dashed orange) \texttt  {4->right = 2} and \texttt  {5->right = 1}, written into null pointers. Riding thread $4\to 2$ is how the walk returns to $2$ with no stack. The real \texttt  {nullptr}s are remembered so every thread can be undone.}}{68}{figure.caption.30}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:c03-threads}{{3.2.1}{68}{The running tree mid-Morris-walk, at the moment \code {cur}~$=4$: two live threads (dashed orange) \code {4->right = 2} and \code {5->right = 1}, written into null pointers. Riding thread $4\to 2$ is how the walk returns to $2$ with no stack. The real \code {nullptr}s are remembered so every thread can be undone}{figure.caption.30}{}}
